Administrative boundaries: data/bound0.rda, data/bound1.rda
------------------------------------------------------------
Source: Thailand administrative level 1 boundaries, Royal Thai Survey
Department (RTSD), distributed by UN OCHA through the Common Operational
Datasets (COD-AB) on the Humanitarian Data Exchange,
https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-tha (release dated 2022-01-21).
Modifications: subset to Health Region 12, selected columns, reprojected to
EPSG:32647; bound0 is the dissolved outer boundary of bound1.
Licence: the current HDX listing of this dataset is licensed under Creative
Commons Attribution for Intergovernmental Organisations 3.0 (CC BY-IGO 3.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/igo/. The metadata embedded in
the 2022 release used here refer instead to the COD/FOD Registry terms of use.


Under-five population: inst/extdata/u5pd.tif
--------------------------------------------
Source: Meta Data for Good and the Center for International Earth Science
Information Network (CIESIN), High Resolution Population Density Maps,
Thailand, children under five, 2020, distributed through the Humanitarian
Data Exchange. Underlying imagery: Maxar Technologies.
Modifications: aggregated by summation to a 520.4038 m grid, reprojected to
EPSG:32647, cropped and masked to Health Region 12.
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.


Health facilities: data/hc12_hos.rda, data/hc12_phc.rda
-------------------------------------------------------
Source: Office of the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Public Health
(Thailand), Government Open Data Services, https://opendata.moph.go.th,
retrieved 2024-12-19 (facility GIS points; provider statistics for B.E. 2563;
health-volunteer statistics for B.E. 2565).
Modifications: subset to Health Region 12, joined across endpoints,
facility identifiers recoded, reprojected to EPSG:32647. Coordinates are
exact; the recoded identifiers are not an anonymisation.
Licence: redistribution terms for these data have not been confirmed.


Travel-time layers: data/hos_iscvec.rda, inst/extdata/hos_iscr.tif,
inst/extdata/phc_iscr.tif (and their *_names.rds companions)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Source: computed by the package author with OSRM (Open Source Routing
Machine) on a 2024 Geofabrik OpenStreetMap extract for Thailand, routed in
December 2024, from the facility locations in hc12_hos and hc12_phc. Each
layer stores travel-time band midpoints in minutes: hospital layers cover
bands up to 180 minutes; primary health centre layers are cut at 60 minutes.
NA marks cells outside the region or beyond the last band.
Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
License (ODbL) 1.0, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright and
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/.
These layers are derived from OpenStreetMap data and from the Ministry of
Public Health facility locations above; their licence status has not been
finally determined. Until it is, treat them as subject to the ODbL 1.0 and
to any terms governing the facility data.
